module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.LimitApproxClose.StageLeg

/-!
# The ring of the affine open being added is the colimit of the distinguished subalgebras

This is the ring half of step (iii) of the one-affine-open step of Tag 07RN.  There the affine
open being added is `Spec B`, the rings at the stages are the fibre products `B_k = B ×_R R_k`
with `B` their filtered colimit, and the distinguished subalgebras are the finite-type ones of
Tag 01Z7 — here, the *charted* ones of `AlgebraicGeometry.IsChartedSubalgebra`.  What is proved
is that `B` is again the filtered colimit of those subalgebras, over the index of pairs
`Stacks.StageSubalgebra`; with `AlgebraicGeometry.isLimitSpecMapCone` that identifies `Spec B` as
the inverse limit of their spectra, which is one of the three restricted cones step (iii) needs.

## The index bridge, and why it is cheap

The ring-level results used here are indexed by the *opposite* of the scheme index:
Tag 01Z0 (`AlgebraicGeometry.nonempty_isColimit_Γ_mapCocone`) produces a cocone over `Jᵒᵖ` for a
diagram of schemes `J ⥤ Scheme`, and the fibre products of
`Stacks.FibreProduct.diagram` inherit that index.  With the schemes indexed by
`Kᵒᵈ` for a preorder `K`, as the structure recording the conclusion of Tag 07RN demands, the
rings are therefore indexed by `(Kᵒᵈ)ᵒᵖ` — which carries no `Preorder` instance, while
`Stacks.StageSubalgebra` needs one.

Transporting an `CategoryTheory.Limits.IsColimit` across the canonical isomorphism of categories
would need that functor to be final.  It is **not needed**: every use the argument makes of the
colimit is *elementwise* — finitely many elements come from one stage, and two elements with the
same image agree at a later stage — and an elementwise statement crosses a bijection of index
objects for free.  So `Stacks.preorderToOpDual` is a plain functor — no finality, no
equivalence — used only to *define* the diagram of rings over `K` as
`Stacks.preorderToOpDual K ⋙ Stacks.FibreProduct.diagram …`; and the colimit enters
`Stacks.StageSubalgebra.nonempty_isColimit_ringCocone` as its two elementwise consequences,
which a consumer reads off the cocone over `(Kᵒᵈ)ᵒᵖ` by taking the index object apart.

## What is proved, and the route

* `Stacks.preorderToOpDual` is the canonical functor from a preorder to the opposite of its order
  dual.  Both functor identities hold because the homs of a preorder are a subsingleton, so the
  opposite's homs are too.

* `Stacks.StageSubalgebra.ringCocone` is the cocone of distinguished subalgebras over the
  colimit ring: the inclusion into the ring at the stage, followed by that stage's leg.
  Naturality is `Stacks.StageSubalgebra.inclusionHom_comp_val` followed by the naturality of the
  given cocone.

* `Stacks.StageSubalgebra.nonempty_isColimit_ringCocone` is the colimit, from the two elementwise
  hypotheses.  Surjectivity: an element of the colimit comes from a stage, and the subalgebra
  generated by its preimage is absorbed into a distinguished one by cofinality.  Separation: two
  elements of one distinguished subalgebra with the same image already agree at a later *stage*,
  and a distinguished subalgebra there absorbing the transported one is a later *pair*.  The
  element chase is `CategoryTheory.Limits.Types.FilteredColimit.isColimitOf'` after reflecting
  along the forgetful functor, exactly as in
  `Stacks.FibreProduct.nonempty_isColimitCocone`.

* `Stacks.StageSubalgebra.nonempty_isColimit_ringCocone_of_isColimit` is the same from an
  `CategoryTheory.Limits.IsColimit` hypothesis, the two elementwise facts being
  `Stacks.FibreProduct.exists_app_eq` and `Stacks.FibreProduct.exists_map_eq`, which are already
  stated for an arbitrary filtered index.

## Universe situation

The stages, the rings and the index of pairs are in the single universe `u`, as the fibre-product
index requires.  The filteredness of the index of pairs is not assumed: it comes from nonemptiness
and directedness, which `Stacks.StageSubalgebra.nonempty` and `Stacks.StageSubalgebra.isDirected`
supply from the two hypotheses on the distinguished subalgebras.

## Transparency gotchas

* The two elementwise hypotheses are stated at the index `K` and *not* as an
  `CategoryTheory.Limits.IsColimit` over `K`, deliberately: the colimit that is available is over
  `(Kᵒᵈ)ᵒᵖ`, and this is the whole reason the index bridge does not have to be an equivalence.

* A later pair is built from a later stage plus a distinguished subalgebra absorbing the
  transported one, and the transition morphism used to transport is reached by `Subsingleton.elim`
  from whichever morphism the separation statement returned; the two are the same morphism, the
  homs of a preorder being a subsingleton.

* The finite generation of a transported subalgebra is `Subalgebra.FG.map`, and of a subalgebra
  generated by one element is `Subalgebra.fg_adjoin_finset` on a singleton finset, which needs a
  `simpa` to match the coercion.

* The separation step closes by `Subtype.ext` on an equality of underlying elements proved
  *pointwise in a `have`*, and not by rewriting the goal: the index of pairs is a `def` for a
  sigma type, so a goal mentioning its projections fails a rewrite's motive check — the same
  shape recorded for `Stacks.StageSubalgebra.ringDiagram`.  The accessors
  `Stacks.StageSubalgebra.stage` and `Stacks.StageSubalgebra.sub` exist for that reason.

## What is NOT done here

Nothing here mentions a scheme.  The cocone of rings at the stages is a hypothesis: this file
does not identify `B` as the colimit of the fibre products, which is
`Stacks.FibreProduct.isColimitCocone`.  Nothing here produces a cone of schemes, a limit, or an
inhabitant of `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.FiniteTypeApproximation`.  Tag 07RN is not proved and no
tag attribute is attached to anything in this file.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07RN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07RN)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01Z7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01Z7)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u

namespace Stacks

/-- The canonical functor from a preorder `K` to the opposite of its order dual, sending `k` to
`op (OrderDual.toDual k)`. -/
def preorderToOpDual (K : Type u) [Preorder K] : K ⥤ (Kᵒᵈ)ᵒᵖ where
  obj k := op (OrderDual.toDual k)
  map {_ _} u := (homOfLE (OrderDual.toDual_le_toDual.mpr (leOfHom u))).op
  map_id _ := Quiver.Hom.unop_inj (Subsingleton.elim _ _)
  map_comp _ _ := Quiver.Hom.unop_inj (Subsingleton.elim _ _)

/-- The functor `preorderToOpDual K` sends `k` to `op (OrderDual.toDual k)`. -/
@[simp]
lemma preorderToOpDual_obj {K : Type u} [Preorder K] (k : K) :
    (preorderToOpDual K).obj k = op (OrderDual.toDual k) := rfl

namespace StageSubalgebra

variable {K : Type u} [Preorder K] {F : K ⥤ CommRingCat.{u}}
  {P : ∀ k : K, Subalgebra ℤ (F.obj k) → Prop} {B : CommRingCat.{u}}
  (τ : F ⟶ (Functor.const K).obj B)

/-- The cocone of distinguished subalgebras over the ring the stages converge to: the inclusion
into the ring at the stage, followed by that stage's leg. -/
def ringCocone : Cocone (ringDiagram F P) where
  pt := B
  ι.app j := CommRingCat.ofHom ((sub j).val : sub j →+* F.obj (stage j)) ≫ τ.app (stage j)
  ι.naturality {j k} u := by
    have h : j ≤ k := leOfHom u
    have hτ : F.map (homOfLE (le_stage h)) ≫ τ.app (stage k) = τ.app (stage j) := by simp
    have key : inclusionHom h ≫ (CommRingCat.ofHom ((sub k).val : sub k →+* F.obj (stage k)) ≫
        τ.app (stage k)) =
        CommRingCat.ofHom ((sub j).val : sub j →+* F.obj (stage j)) ≫ τ.app (stage j) := by
      rw [← Category.assoc, ← inclusionHom_comp_val h, Category.assoc, hτ]
    simpa using key

/-- The leg of `ringCocone τ` at `j` is the inclusion of `sub j` into the ring at `stage j`,
followed by `τ.app (stage j)`. -/
@[simp]
lemma ringCocone_ι_app (j : StageSubalgebra F P) :
    (ringCocone (P := P) τ).ι.app j =
      CommRingCat.ofHom ((sub j).val : sub j →+* F.obj (stage j)) ≫ τ.app (stage j) := rfl

/-- **The ring is the filtered colimit of the distinguished subalgebras.** If every
distinguished subalgebra is finitely generated, every finitely generated subalgebra lies in a
distinguished one, every element of `B` comes from some stage, and two elements of a stage with
the same image in `B` become equal at a later stage, then `ringCocone τ` is a colimit cocone. -/
lemma nonempty_isColimit_ringCocone [Nonempty K] [IsDirected K (· ≤ ·)]
    (hfg : ∀ (k : K) (A : Subalgebra ℤ (F.obj k)), P k A → A.FG)
    (hcof : ∀ (k : K) (C : Subalgebra ℤ (F.obj k)), C.FG → ∃ A, P k A ∧ C ≤ A)
    (hsurj : ∀ x : B, ∃ (k : K) (y : F.obj k), τ.app k y = x)
    (hsep : ∀ (k : K) (y z : F.obj k), τ.app k y = τ.app k z →
      ∃ (k' : K) (v : k ⟶ k'), F.map v y = F.map v z) :
    Nonempty (IsColimit (ringCocone (P := P) τ)) := by
  classical
  have hne : Nonempty (StageSubalgebra F P) :=
    nonempty fun k ↦ (hcof k ⊥ Subalgebra.fg_bot).imp fun _ h ↦ h.1
  have hdir : IsDirected (StageSubalgebra F P) (· ≤ ·) := isDirected hfg hcof
  have : ReflectsFilteredColimits (forget CommRingCat) :=
    ⟨fun _ ↦ reflectsColimitsOfShape_of_reflectsIsomorphisms⟩
  refine ReflectsColimit.reflects (F := forget CommRingCat)
    (Types.FilteredColimit.isColimitOf' (ringDiagram F P ⋙ forget CommRingCat)
      ((forget CommRingCat).mapCocone (ringCocone (P := P) τ)) (fun x ↦ ?_) (fun j a a' h ↦ ?_))
  · obtain ⟨k, y, hy⟩ := hsurj x
    have hfgy : (Algebra.adjoin ℤ ({y} : Set (F.obj k))).FG := by
      simpa using Subalgebra.fg_adjoin_finset ({y} : Finset (F.obj k))
    obtain ⟨A, hA, hyA⟩ := hcof k _ hfgy
    exact ⟨⟨k, A, hA⟩, ⟨y, hyA (Algebra.subset_adjoin (by simp))⟩, hy.symm⟩
  · have h' : τ.app (stage j) ((sub j).val a) = τ.app (stage j) ((sub j).val a') := h
    obtain ⟨k', v, hv⟩ := hsep (stage j) ((sub j).val a) ((sub j).val a') h'
    obtain ⟨A', hA', hle⟩ := hcof k' (transport (leOfHom v) (sub j))
      ((hfg _ _ j.2.2).map _)
    have hjk : j ≤ (⟨k', A', hA'⟩ : StageSubalgebra F P) := ⟨leOfHom v, hle⟩
    have key : ∀ x : sub j, (inclusionAlgHom hjk x).1 = F.map v x.1 := fun x ↦ by
      rw [Subsingleton.elim v (homOfLE (le_stage hjk))]
      rfl
    exact ⟨⟨k', A', hA'⟩, homOfLE hjk,
      Subtype.ext ((key a).trans (hv.trans (key a').symm))⟩

/-- **The ring is the filtered colimit of the distinguished subalgebras**, from a colimit cocone
of the rings at the stages.  The two elementwise facts are
`Stacks.FibreProduct.exists_app_eq` and `Stacks.FibreProduct.exists_map_eq`. -/
lemma nonempty_isColimit_ringCocone_of_isColimit [Nonempty K] [IsDirected K (· ≤ ·)]
    (hfg : ∀ (k : K) (A : Subalgebra ℤ (F.obj k)), P k A → A.FG)
    (hcof : ∀ (k : K) (C : Subalgebra ℤ (F.obj k)), C.FG → ∃ A, P k A ∧ C ≤ A)
    (hc : IsColimit (Cocone.mk B τ)) :
    Nonempty (IsColimit (ringCocone (P := P) τ)) :=
  nonempty_isColimit_ringCocone τ hfg hcof
    (fun x ↦ FibreProduct.exists_app_eq hc x)
    (fun _ y z hyz ↦ (FibreProduct.exists_map_eq hc y z hyz).imp fun _ h ↦ h)

end StageSubalgebra

end Stacks
